WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.960
- So I was raised in a bit
of a conservative family

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.090
where women shouldn't be climbing

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.810
and traveling on their own.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:10.180
So coming to Dubai really
helped me find all these sports

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.075
that I enjoy doing.

00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:14.500
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.280
You have to reconnect to
nature, to Mother Earth

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.780
to feel better about yourself.

00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:24.630
(dramatic music)

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.430
- My name is Mark Beaumont
and I'm an endurance athlete.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.290
With the current world record
for cycling around the planet.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.200
Seeking adventures and finding stories is

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.290
what I'm most passionate about.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.740
Ever since I can remember,

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.323
I've had that sense of
curiosity about the world.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.393
This time I've come to Dubai.

00:00:47.688 --> 00:00:50.110
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.390
Here I'm meeting Ghida,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.410
to hear how her love of the
outdoors and adventure sports

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:55.800
has hugely helped her,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.250
both physically and mentally.

00:01:00.007 --> 00:01:03.830
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.820
What have you got planned?

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.420
What do think we can
get up to in the next?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.660
- So, I'm gonna take you wakeboarding and

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.810
we're gonna go to Hatta.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.900
We're gonna kayak in a dam.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.730
And we're gonna hike a
little bit and maybe camp.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.075
- And is that still in
the desert or is that

00:01:18.075 --> 00:01:19.283
a completely different terrain?

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:20.710
- It's a completely different terrain.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.246
- Amazing.

00:01:22.246 --> 00:01:23.870
(upbeat music)

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.920
- [Guida] Be careful.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.810
- It's not often I try something

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.294
that I've never done before.

00:01:33.294 --> 00:01:34.319
- Really?

00:01:34.319 --> 00:01:36.310
- Wakeboarding's not big in Scotland.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.950
Maybe 'cause it's too cold.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:41.090
- So Mark, when the boat starts moving,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.220
you feel it and you just glide with it.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.110
And then you just look
at the boat and enjoy.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.780
I've always been active in Dubai,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.410
but then I had an
incident where I fractured

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.120
my hip and I couldn't
do anything for a year.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.050
And this was the turning point for me.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.720
This is what made me become
a more adventurous person.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.640
I thought that I have to try everything,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.230
I couldn't do in that year.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.080
And this is where my journey started.

00:02:09.822 --> 00:02:11.359
- Ah, that doesn't look too easy.

00:02:11.359 --> 00:02:13.770
(laughing)

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.380
Pretty amazing place to go
wakeboarding for the first time.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.213
What a backdrop!

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:22.558
Ooh wee!

00:02:22.558 --> 00:02:24.847
- The water is nice!

00:02:24.847 --> 00:02:26.014
You can do it!

00:02:28.415 --> 00:02:29.944
Yeah!

00:02:29.944 --> 00:02:30.777
Stand up!

00:02:32.855 --> 00:02:33.688
Woo-hoo!

00:02:35.061 --> 00:02:37.811
(dramatic music)

00:02:39.646 --> 00:02:40.896
He's a natural!

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.461
He's doing really great
for the first time.

00:02:44.461 --> 00:02:47.211
(dramatic music)

00:02:53.287 --> 00:02:54.369
- That was incredible!

00:02:54.369 --> 00:02:56.677
- [Guida] So good! You
are a natural! (laughs)

00:02:56.677 --> 00:02:57.923
- I loved it.

00:02:57.923 --> 00:02:59.260
That is incredible.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.235
My arms!

00:03:00.235 --> 00:03:01.089
- [Guida] Yeah.

00:03:01.089 --> 00:03:02.339
- My arms hurt.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.153
- [Guida Voiceover] I really think

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:09.042
that being healthy
physically is very important

00:03:09.042 --> 00:03:14.042
but I really focus on being
healthy mentally more.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.840
Anytime I feel down or
I feel super anxious,

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.940
I just pack my bags and
travel to the mountains

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.490
or go camping or just
be in the outdoors and

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.703
reconnect with myself.

00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:29.834
Thank you!

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.040
As someone who suffers from anxiety,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.437
being outdoors and being
active help me so much

00:03:37.437 --> 00:03:38.643
and it still does.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.100
- [Mark] I mean you feel
like you're a million miles

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.630
from Dubai here.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.463
- [Ghida] I know.

00:03:45.463 --> 00:03:47.070
- [Mark] Skyscrapers to mountains.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.510
- [Ghida] To natural skyscrapers!

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.360
- [Mark Voiceover] I think
what sport's given you know

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.170
is the fact that you're not
worrying about tomorrow.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.180
You're not thinking too
much about the past.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.730
You're absolutely stuck in
that moment and she's like

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.630
passionate about sharing that journey.

00:04:03.329 --> 00:04:07.162
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.130
It gets dark pretty quickly.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:28.963
- [Ghida] It's nice.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:32.654
- [Mark] And this looks
tiny from the valley floor.

00:04:32.654 --> 00:04:33.487
- [Ghida] Yes!

00:04:33.487 --> 00:04:34.490
- Look at it!

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.323
- Wow!

00:04:35.323 --> 00:04:36.790
- Top of the world.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.623
Nice view.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.440
Adventure sports and
finding them is ultimately

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.840
from our time together that's
kind of created your identity.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.673
It's kind of who you are.

00:04:47.673 --> 00:04:51.247
- I know that my aim is to
get more and more people

00:04:51.247 --> 00:04:53.370
in the outdoors.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.470
Like this is something I want to do.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:58.940
Being active and being closer
to nature will make you

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.740
a better person mentally and physically.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.351
- I've absolutely loved this.

00:05:03.351 --> 00:05:04.870
And do you know what the coolest part?

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.530
You know, you've been so
honest about your journey.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.180
You know what all these
adventures have done for you.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.530
So thank you.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:12.363
And I hope we can do some more.

00:05:12.363 --> 00:05:14.259
- [Ghida] It's my pleasure.

00:05:14.259 --> 00:05:17.092
(dramatic music)

